chu and he  transforms seemingly against his will in  this spot we see him shouting whilst  kicking a mirror and if you watched our  first trailer breakdown then you'll know  that mirrors appeared throughout it  there was a scene where steven left the  museum at night and two of his  reflections remained behind likely  symbolizing mark and jake later on in  the bathroom scene which we know is  where moonlight fights a jackal you can  also catch a reflection standing there  staring at him i believe that this is  mark constantly trying to get out and  that he'll appear in mirrors along with  jake talking to him this will give oscar  isaacs the chance to do a sort of norman  osborne thing where he goes back and  forth in a mirror and has scenes  wrestling with his personalities mark  seems to be a mystery that steven  doesn't know about and therefore makes  sense that he's completely repressing  him the phone call that he had in the  first trailer brought this up and it  also had an image of either a crocodile  or alligator which somewhat ties into  our theory about what's going on with  arthur harrow now we get a good look at  harrow in this tv spot who seems to have  a mysterious connection to steven in the  comics arthur harrow carried out human  experiments and he'd done this dating  all the way back to the holocaust in the  80s he was working on quote-unquote pain  research and he was helped by a  mysterious organization which led him  into conflict with moon knight show  vision seems to be markedly different  and is possible that he's the embodiment  of a god much like how moon knight is at  one point we see moving scales on his  arm and if you look at the top of these  they have crocodile heads on them this  could be the god amit who had the head  of a crocodile and it was deemed unruly  by anubis and he got nicknamed the  davara of souls in the comics moon i  clashed with a character called dr remit  who was really amit so there is  precedent there in the source material  anubis the god of the dead would also  weigh a dead person's heart to see if  they were worthy to enter the underworld  and the scales could be referring to  that harrow seems to have special  abilities as we see him with the scepter  and potentially he's the character  shooting the purple lightning into the  sky purple magic has appeared throughout  the mcu and we've often discussed how it  pulls from the dark dimension this was  shown at the end of doctor strange and  also on agatha harkness who tap into the  dimension when casting spells now harrow  can also hear the voices in steven's  head so yeah that's the direction i  think they'll be going a crocodile also  appeared in the first trailer when we  could catch one in the museum and yeah  god amit it's him puns are still golden  now there is the possibility that he's a  combination of other moonlight  characters as harrow hasn't really  appeared that much in the comics ethan  hawk has also stated that he looked at  cult leaders like david koresh to mold  his character and from the first trailer  we know people are willing to bow before  him in a recent ish issue of moon knight  number 189 moonai tangled with a cult  leader called the sun king who was an  avatar on earth either way there's heavy  themes towards gods in the teasers and  in the recent runs konchu has been  expanded upon along with the rest of the  egyptian pantheon they are revealed to  have been in the other void and they  basically just use humans as their  playthings seeing gods on earth using  humans as avatars to fight would be  pretty exciting and really expand upon  the egyptian myths we also catch shots  of stephen in egypt and in a temple  which might be his mcu origin or he  could be returning to egypt in order to  fight arthur harrow now there's a reason  that some of the show takes place in the  british museum as it houses the world's  largest collection of egyptian antiques  a key item could be there which is why  both harrow and moonai are there and it  could be moonai trying to stop harrow  from obtaining something to unlock the  pyramids pyramid iconography appears  throughout the trailer and when we get  that cool cape shot you can also catch a  pyramid to the right of it it looks a  bit like the glass one at the louvre and  i'm sure that this is probably a real  location so let me know if you're  familiar with it inside it there's a  pyramid and yet pyramids permits  pyramids when he transforms we can also  catch the top of a spire which looks  like a pyramid and as i've been saying  it's all connected now museums make up a  lot of the teasers and interestingly the  british museum was also used for the  illuminati base in the multiverse of  madness trailer it seems the theme of  phase 4 is museums with the eternals  partly taking place in the natural  history one located in london blade also  came across dane whitman there in the  post credits scene so there's  potentially lots of callbacks all tying  in with museums now we know from the  press release that stephen will also don  has missed a night costume at some point  and it's going to be really interesting  to see how this is tied in potentially  it might be the suit of one of his many  personalities i'd love it if each one  had their own costume we also learned in  these releases that moon knight will be  a lot more brutal as kevin feige has  stated it pushes the boundaries of  violence in the mcu this could open up  the creatures of the night aspect of the  marvel universe as we know blade and  black knight are coming that pretty much  wraps it up and what i love about the  trailer is that moon knight looks unlike  anything disney and marvel have put out  which makes it so exciting as the movies  head into wild fan service which isn't  necessarily a bad thing this seems to be  off doing its own sort of thing i  absolutely love the teaser and the moon  iconography in it we get mk catching a  moonerang and there's also a moon that's  the same shape in the night sky there's  an awesome cape shot which looks like it  and the teaser ends with him jumping  across the sky with the moon in the  background m-o-o-n that spells moon and  i love this new teaser did you catch the  pyramid by the moon rang is there  anything we missed let me know your punk  in the comment section below we are in a  competition right now and giving away  three copies of the june box set on the  28th of feb and all you have to do to be  on the chance of winning is like the  video make sure you subscribe with  notifications on and drop a comment  below with your thoughts on the teaser  we pick the comments at random at the  end of the month and the winners of the  last one are on screen right now so if  that's you then message me on twitter at  heavyspoilers if you want something else  to watch then make sure you check out  our breakdown of the doctor strange in  the multiverse of madness trailer which  will be linked on screen right now we go  over everything that we found in it and  talk about all the theories we have on  the movie so definitely go head over  there right after this without the way  thanks for sticking through the video  i've been paul you've been the best i'll  see you next time take care peace

